This repository contains only the Debian recipe for cv181x-sodoport.

Linux source and the six board/media enablement patches are maintained as
commits in https://github.com/slopization/linux-cv181x-sodoport, based on
upstream torvalds/linux v7.1. Source main aggregates stacked patch branches.
Do not reapply those hardware patches from Debian quilt packaging.

Shared slopization/debian-ci CI assembles an immutable source SHA and an
independently pinned recipe SHA, creates the orig tarball from the source
Git archive, and builds the 3.0 (quilt) source package. No uscan, gbp import,
generated-source branches, or Git pushes are used. debian/patches is reserved
for Debian-only changes; its series is currently empty.

Cross-building uses a native amd64 trixie chroot with sbuild --build amd64
--host riscv64 --arch-all. This includes linux-source (Architecture: all)
as well as image/header packages and their meta-packages (riscv64).

The initial board configuration and DTS seed came from the local
/root/uboot/sg2002 Alpine package draft. The checked-in board config remains
the effective build input. Base and fragment configuration inputs are kept
under debian/config; regenerate against an existing Linux source tree with:

  debian/scripts/update-config.sh /path/to/linux

See the repository README for the dispatch API, recipe pinning, provenance,
package outputs, and separate manual publishing policy.
